      "claim": "All L1 gold records report absolute or systemic bioavailability values or qualitative outcomes at or above about 35% (alfuzosin 49%, rigosertib 35%/34.8%, GDC-0810 ~45%, indomethacin 76-80%, midodrine 90-100%, colchicine 44-55%, omeprazole ~100%, 5-HTP 49%, loratadine good), so the gold evidence direction uniformly supports F >= 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C01", "C02", "C03", "C04", "C05", "C06", "C07", "C08", "C09", "C10", "C11", "C12", "C13", "C14", "C15", "C16", "C17", "C18", "C19", "C20", "C21"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The closest gold context, alfuzosin (dimethoxy-aminoheteroaromatic with amide side chain), has F=49% under fed conditions; the query shares dimethoxyheteroaromatic and amide motifs, supporting transfer to F >= 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C01", "C18", "C33", "C35"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 records demonstrate gut-wall efflux for analogs with 2,4-diaminopyrimidine/quinazoline and chloro-indole amide motifs (prazosin/BCRP, UK-338,003/PGP, compounds 25/26), and C70 shows BCRP inhibition can increase oral bioavailability; however, none of these records reports an absolute F value, and efflux substrate status alone does not affirmatively establish F < 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C65", "C66", "C67", "C68", "C70", "C71", "C72", "C73", "C74", "C75", "C76"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The low physicochemical prior (high MW/TPSA/logP, low Fsp3) is an uncertain prior calibrated to F=20%, not affirmative endpoint evidence; no transferable direct low-F record supports F < 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C07", "C10", "C12", "C32"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "gut_wall_efflux_intestinal_metabolism",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "contradictory",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C65", "C66", "C67", "C68", "C69", "C70", "C71", "C72", "C73", "C74", "C75", "C76"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct query-specific absolute oral bioavailability measurement is available.",
    "No query-specific efflux or intestinal metabolism measurement is available; L5 records are for analogs with moderate transfer likelihood.",
    "No query-specific solubility or permeability measurement is available.",
    "The query has no reported external condition (fasted/fed, modified release, disease), limiting direct transfer of condition-specific gold contexts.",
    "L5 efflux records do not report absolute F values, so they cannot affirmatively establish F < 20%.",
    "The query is larger and more lipophilic than the closest gold context (alfuzosin), so structural transfer is imperfect."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L5 adds mechanistic gut-wall efflux evidence for structurally related motifs, but no direct F<20% outcome and no query-specific measurement. L1/L2 gold and context records uniformly support F>=20%, with the closest context (alfuzosin) at 49%. The low physicochemical prior and efflux mechanism are insufficient to overturn the high prediction; prediction remains high with moderate confidence."
}

